    "body": "## Overview\n\n`top_logprobs=-1` means \"every candidate\" and Chat Completions returns them all, but `/v1/responses` with `include=[\"message.output_text.logprobs\"]` returns an empty `top_logprobs` list for each token. The request is accepted and the engine still computes full-vocabulary logprobs (`SamplingParams.logprobs == -1`); `_topk_logprobs` then stops at `i >= top_logprobs`, which is true on the first item when the value is -1. I made that loop treat -1 as no limit, the way `_get_top_logprobs` does for chat.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `top_logprobs=-1` on `/v1/responses` returns every candidate per token, streaming and non-streaming (both go through `_create_response_logprobs`).\n- Positive values and `0` behave as before.\n\n## Validation\n\nNoticed while reading the Responses serving code next to the chat one. No GPU here, so I called `_create_response_logprobs` directly with a three-candidate step:\n\n```python\nserving = OpenAIServingResponses.__new__(OpenAIServingResponses)\nserving.return_tokens_as_token_ids = False\nstep = {i: Logprob(logprob=-float(i), decoded_token=t) for i, t in enumerate(\"abc\", 1)}\nfor k in (2, -1):\n    (lp,) = serving._create_response_logprobs([1], [step], MagicMock(), top_logprobs=k)\n    print(f\"top_logprobs={k}:\", [t.token for t in lp.top_logprobs])\n```\n\n```text\n# main (03091e28b)            # this PR\ntop_logprobs=2: ['a', 'b']    top_logprobs=2: ['a', 'b']\ntop_logprobs=-1: []           top_logprobs=-1: ['a', 'b', 'c']\n```\n\nAdded `test_response_logprobs_honor_top_logprobs` (-1, 2, 0); the -1 case fails on main. `pytest tests/entrypoints/openai/responses/test_serving_responses.py` passes locally, ruff is clean. I did not run a live server.\n\n## Details\n\nNot a duplicate as far as I can tell: #55717 fixes the same -1 handling for `/v1/completions` and doesn't touch the Responses path, and I didn't find an issue or PR for this one.\n\nAI assistance was used to find and prepare this change.\n\n\n---\n\n<detai